{"candidates": [{"content": {"parts": [{"text": "Please perform an OD600 to CFU/mL calibration on our two positive control (BBa_I20270) and two negative control (BBa_R0040) overnight cultures using the following protocol:\n\n1. Measure the OD600 of each overnight culture on a plate reader, diluting into the linear range with LB + chloramphenicol media as needed and subtracting the blank baseline.\n2. Prepare three independent 1 mL dilutions at target OD600 = 0.1 in LB + chloramphenicol for each of the 4 cultures (12 starting samples total). Verify that the final OD600 of each dilution is 0.1.\n3. For each of the 12 starting samples, perform serial dilutions in LB + chloramphenicol as follows (vortex each tube 5\u201310 seconds between steps; do not pipette up and down):\n   - Dilution 1: 100 \u00b5L starting sample into 1900 \u00b5L media\n   - Dilution 2: 100 \u00b5L of Dilution 1 into 1900 \u00b5L media\n   - Dilution 3: 100 \u00b5L of Dilution 2 into 1900 \u00b5L media\n   - Dilution 4: 100 \u00b5L of Dilution 3 into 900 \u00b5L media\n   - Dilution 5: 100 \u00b5L of Dilution 4 into 900 \u00b5L media\n4. Aseptically spread 100 \u00b5L of Dilutions 3, 4, and 5 onto individual LB agar + chloramphenicol plates (36 plates total).\n5. Incubate the plates at 37 \u00b0C for 18\u201320 hours.\n6. Count colonies on all plates containing fewer than 300 colonies and calculate the resulting CFU/mL for an OD600 = 0.1 culture by applying the respective dilution factors. Return the raw colony counts and calculated CFU/mL values to us.", "thoughtSignature": ""}], "role": "model"}, "finishReason": "STOP", "index": 0}], "usageMetadata": {"promptTokenCount": 1445, "candidatesTokenCount": 448, "totalTokenCount": 2657, "promptTokensDetails": [{"modality": "TEXT", "tokenCount": 1445}], "thoughtsTokenCount": 764, "serviceTier": "standard"}, "modelVersion": "gemini-3.6-flash", "responseId": "zWf3avz7Leen1MkP1qiFkQ4"}